Later on Thursday evening, I am at home in my flat.
I sit on the sofa and take my mobile phone.
I start a video call with my family in Mexico.
In Berlin it is already eight o'clock in the evening, but in Mexico it is only midday.
My mother answers immediately.
"Hello Maya, how are you?" she asks.
"Very good," I say.
"I played badminton today."
"I talked with Timo and Lena after the game."
"I told them my whole story."
"Your whole story?" my mother asks.
"Yes," I answer.
"I talked about the job, the papers and my first weeks here."
My mother smiles.
"We missed you so much in January," she says.
"I missed you too," I say.
"But I have never heard your story," my mother says.
"What exactly did you say?"
